  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649200",
      "title": "Component Composition: The special \"children\" Prop [Core Concept]",
      "sourceHash": "af6b7084aa3615707d729bb6e5f93d98775207b5e62676f68ab79974e3b00eb0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "Okay, that's enough about folder structures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 7.65,
          "en": "Let's continue working on that app and let's start working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.65,
          "end": 11.85,
          "en": "on that next big feature, which is this interactive section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.85,
          "end": 13.95,
          "en": "at the bottom of the website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.95,
          "end": 17.61,
          "en": "And let's therefore start adding some new components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.61,
          "end": 18.93,
          "en": "And I wanna start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.93,
          "end": 23.61,
          "en": "by creating a new component for these tab buttons here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.61,
          "end": 26.55,
          "en": "And for that in the app.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.55,
          "end": 30.39,
          "en": "in this main area I'll add another section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.39,
          "end": 34.56,
          "en": "after this first CoreConcepts section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.56,
          "end": 39.56,
          "en": "And this next section should receive an ID of examples",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 42.723,
          "en": "which again will be required for styling purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.86,
          "end": 46.35,
          "en": "And in there I'll then add a h2 tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.35,
          "end": 48.153,
          "en": "where I'll say examples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.44,
          "end": 52.8,
          "en": "And below that we can use the built-in menu element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.8,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "which is a default HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 58.02,
          "en": "even though you might not have used it too often",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.02,
          "end": 59.52,
          "en": "up to this point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 64.02,
          "en": "which can be used to create a list of buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.02,
          "end": 67.62,
          "en": "And that's exactly what I wanna have here for my tabs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.62,
          "end": 70.28999999999999,
          "en": "I wanna have a list of buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.28999999999999,
          "end": 72.3,
          "en": "Therefore, of course, we could add a bunch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.3,
          "end": 76.92,
          "en": "of list items with buttons like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.92,
          "end": 79.08,
          "en": "But since we have this repetition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "we could also just create a new component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 85.17,
          "en": "And indeed, that is what I will do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.17,
          "end": 88.59,
          "en": "So I'll add a new component file next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.59,
          "end": 91.89,
          "en": "to the CoreConcept.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 95.163,
          "en": "And I'll name it TapButton,jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.05,
          "end": 99,
          "en": "And in there I'll export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99,
          "end": 102.06,
          "en": "a default function called TabButton",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.06,
          "end": 104.67,
          "en": "because that should be my component name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.67,
          "end": 108.36,
          "en": "And in there I'll return this JSX code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.36,
          "end": 110.253,
          "en": "so this list item with a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 115.05,
          "en": "But now here's where things will get interesting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.05,
          "end": 117.9,
          "en": "because it would be great if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.9,
          "end": 121.98,
          "en": "in the app.jsx file, we could use this tab button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.98,
          "end": 126.98,
          "en": "in this menu like this with opening and closing tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.43,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "And between those tags, our button text, like Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 136.233,
          "en": "to show the component related example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.1,
          "end": 138.72,
          "en": "It would be nice if we could use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.72,
          "end": 141,
          "en": "our custom component like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141,
          "end": 144.54,
          "en": "And as a side note, for this TabButton component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.54,
          "end": 149.28,
          "en": "to be available here, you of course, have to add this import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.28,
          "end": 152.49,
          "en": "where you import this TabButton component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.49,
          "end": 156.303,
          "en": "from your TabButton,jsx file in the Components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.65,
          "end": 159.18,
          "en": "But with that, it would be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.18,
          "end": 161.52,
          "en": "if we could use it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.52,
          "end": 164.88,
          "en": "But at the moment, if I save this, you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.88,
          "end": 166.77,
          "en": "that I don't get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.77,
          "end": 170.13,
          "en": "but I also don't see any buttons down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.13,
          "end": 172.05,
          "en": "It's an empty field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.05,
          "end": 175.89,
          "en": "And I also don't see the text Components anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.89,
          "end": 179.463,
          "en": "down here, even though I have this text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.87,
          "end": 184.68,
          "en": "But this text is basically ignored by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.68,
          "end": 188.91,
          "en": "because if I pass something between component opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.91,
          "end": 193.91,
          "en": "and closing text, this content is by default not output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.73,
          "end": 199.73,
          "en": "on the page because React would not know where to output it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 200.01,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "I mean after all, you are telling React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 206.43,
          "en": "that your custom component should be output on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 206.43,
          "end": 210.36,
          "en": "So how would React know what to do with this text here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.36,
          "end": 213.93,
          "en": "Well, for that we can go to this custom component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.93,
          "end": 216.57,
          "en": "this TabButton component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216.57,
          "end": 218.86,
          "en": "And again, accept props in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 219.75,
          "end": 224.34,
          "en": "because every custom component will receive props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 224.34,
          "end": 227.25,
          "en": "Even if you're not setting any attributes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 227.25,
          "end": 231.09,
          "en": "React will still give you such a props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.09,
          "end": 235.38,
          "en": "It will just be an object that's pretty empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 235.38,
          "end": 238.95,
          "en": "but actually not entirely empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.95,
          "end": 243.27,
          "en": "Instead there is one prop which you will always get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.27,
          "end": 246.633,
          "en": "the special, built-in children prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.13,
          "end": 251.79,
          "en": "This is a prop that's set by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 251.79,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "and it's a prop that's not set with help of attributes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 259.44,
          "en": "So you don't set children like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 259.44,
          "end": 263.49,
          "en": "Instead, this children prop here simply refers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 263.49,
          "end": 267.273,
          "en": "to the content between your component text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 268.53,
          "end": 273.24,
          "en": "So the children prop contains whichever content you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 273.24,
          "end": 277.02,
          "en": "between your component text, and that can simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 277.02,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "be some text as we have it here, but it could also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 285.183,
          "en": "be some complex JSX structure instead if needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 286.11,
          "end": 288.453,
          "en": "But here we just need that text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 289.716,
          "end": 291.78,
          "en": "And therefore, in the custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 291.78,
          "end": 296.78,
          "en": "you can output that content with props.children, or again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 298.47,
          "end": 301.5,
          "en": "by using object destructuring here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 301.5,
          "end": 304.11,
          "en": "and by pulling out the children property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 304.11,
          "end": 308.07,
          "en": "and storing it in its own variable you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 308.07,
          "end": 310.413,
          "en": "so that you can use it just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 311.76,
          "end": 314.28,
          "en": "With that, if you save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 314.28,
          "end": 317.16,
          "en": "you now see the text Components here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 317.16,
          "end": 321.54,
          "en": "and you also see that it is a button that can be clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 321.54,
          "end": 324.72,
          "en": "Of course it doesn't do anything at the moment when clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 324.72,
          "end": 326.61,
          "en": "but it is a clickable button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 326.61,
          "end": 329.55,
          "en": "And you can see that Components text here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 329.55,
          "end": 334.55,
          "en": "which clearly proves that this children prop here works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 335.22,
          "end": 338.55,
          "en": "And this way of building Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 338.55,
          "end": 342.6,
          "en": "where your Components can wrap other Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 342.6,
          "end": 347.6,
          "en": "or other content is called component composition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 347.67,
          "end": 350.73,
          "en": "And this approach here is not better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 350.73,
          "end": 353.19,
          "en": "than using a component like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 353.19,
          "end": 357.69,
          "en": "Instead, it simply depends on the exact use case you have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 357.69,
          "end": 360.15,
          "en": "For the CoreConcept component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 360.15,
          "end": 364.23,
          "en": "it made sense to receive multiple attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 364.23,
          "end": 368.88,
          "en": "that configured the different parts of this component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 368.88,
          "end": 371.04,
          "en": "because we just need different pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 371.04,
          "end": 373.23,
          "en": "of data that should be injected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 373.23,
          "end": 375.573,
          "en": "into the markup of this component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 376.62,
          "end": 378.96,
          "en": "For the TabButton, on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 378.96,
          "end": 382.38,
          "en": "it maybe makes more sense to use this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 382.38,
          "end": 386.7,
          "en": "because that's also how you would use a regular button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 386.7,
          "end": 387.84,
          "en": "and therefore this might be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 387.84,
          "end": 390.99,
          "en": "more convenient and recognizable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 390.99,
          "end": 395.4,
          "en": "We definitely could have also gone for a different approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 395.4,
          "end": 400.4,
          "en": "and maybe added a label prop like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 401.01,
          "end": 404.01,
          "en": "and we could have then used this label prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 404.01,
          "end": 405.273,
          "en": "inside of the TabButton.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 406.32,
          "end": 408.87,
          "en": "We could have done this as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 408.87,
          "end": 410.85,
          "en": "And if you save all these files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 410.85,
          "end": 413.04,
          "en": "after switching to this label prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 413.04,
          "end": 416.88,
          "en": "instead you get the same result as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 416.88,
          "end": 419.64,
          "en": "So both approaches work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 419.64,
          "end": 423.33,
          "en": "and there is no better or worse approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 423.33,
          "end": 427.11,
          "en": "Instead it comes down to personal preference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 427.11,
          "end": 430.29,
          "en": "but you of course must be aware of both approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 430.29,
          "end": 434.67,
          "en": "because you'll see both approaches in actual projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 434.67,
          "end": 438.57,
          "en": "And as mentioned, you might prefer this approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 438.57,
          "end": 442.44,
          "en": "in certain situations since it might be easier to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 442.44,
          "end": 446.1,
          "en": "in certain situations or simply because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 446.1,
          "end": 449.4,
          "en": "in some situations it might be closer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 449.4,
          "end": 453.03,
          "en": "to the HTML code you would be writing otherwise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 453.03,
          "end": 456.06,
          "en": "if you would not be using React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 456.06,
          "end": 459.15,
          "en": "Therefore here, I'll stick to this children prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 459.15,
          "end": 461.37,
          "en": "and to this composition approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 461.37,
          "end": 463.92,
          "en": "but both approaches are valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 463.92,
          "end": 466.89,
          "en": "And with that, we got our first button here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 466.89,
          "end": 469.71,
          "en": "Now we can of course quickly add more buttons",
